(defmodule lsp
  "**Language servers** — the editor as an LSP client: completion, definitions and references,
hover and signature help, code actions, rename and formatting, the diagnostics a server
publishes, semantic colours and code lenses.

The context's details live under `src/lsp/`: the JSON-RPC client a server is spoken to through
(`lsp/client`), what is said on the wire (`lsp/protocol`) and the request kinds
(`lsp/requests`), the servers a buffer has and starting them (`lsp/servers`), the commands
(`lsp/commands`), semantic tokens (`lsp/semantic`) and code lenses (`lsp/lens`). A server's
diagnostics land in the `diagnostics` context's store, where the checker's do.

Other contexts reach a server through the commands — `M-.`, `M-?`, `C-c C-a` and the rest, by
name — and through the functions below. Loading this module loads the parts that register at
load: the autostart and the text push (`lsp/commands`), the semantic-token and code-lens
layers."
  ;; loaded with the context: each registers its idle job, event handler or paint layer at load
  (:use lsp/commands :only []) ; autostart, the text push, signature help, the `:lsp-…` events
  (:use lsp/semantic :only []) ; semantic tokens: the idle ask, the carry, the paint layer
  (:use lsp/lens :only [])) ; code lenses: rows above their lines

(defdelegate connection (m file) lsp/client :as lsp-conn)
(defdelegate merged-diagnostics (m path) lsp/servers :as ed-lsp-merged-diags)
(defdelegate code-action (m key) lsp/commands :as cmd-lsp-code-action)
(defdelegate stop-all (m) lsp/servers :as ed-lsp-stop-all)
